{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, while minimizing thickness expansion to 13.1% after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalable production for practical battery applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables scalable production for 2 Ah NCM811 pouch cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing critical mechanical and electrochemical instability challenges in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ brain cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 mark distinct repression mechanisms. This resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states defined by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal epigenomic atlas provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the mechanisms of Angelman syndrome, caused by UBE3A loss. Using gain- and loss-of-function mutations and proteomics, it identifies asparagine synthetase (ASNS) as a UBE3A substrate. ASNS overabundance in Ube3a-null mice and human neurons activates stress signaling, reduces neuronal protein synthesis, and rescues microcephaly and behavioral deficits when corrected genetically. The findings suggest persistent neuronal stress signaling underlies Angelman syndrome phenotypes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ASNS is a UBE3A substrate with increased abundance in Ube3a-null mice and human neurons",
    "ASNS overabundance activates stress signaling and reduces neuronal protein synthesis",
    "Genetic correction of ASNS overabundance rescues microcephaly and behavioral deficits"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies a specific stress signaling pathway activated by UBE3A loss that contributes to Angelman syndrome pathophysiology, providing a potential therapeutic target."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduces ILC3 numbers and increases enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreases PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the scale of foreign intervention on U.S. campuses following an FBI agent's initiative to combat such activities. The research assesses the problem's scope through the agent's ongoing analysis. Findings indicate significant foreign involvement, though the exact extent remains unclear due to limited data.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The FBI agent initiated NIH's campaign against foreign intervention on U.S. campuses",
    "The agent's analysis reveals substantial foreign activity on campus",
    "Exact problem scale remains uncertain due to insufficient data"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides insight into the intersection of domestic security and international influence in educational settings, highlighting gaps in understanding foreign campus engagement."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record efficiencies of 24.84% in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study isolates a thermophilic archaeon, Methanoglobus dolicholipophagus AA-75, capable of lipotrophic methanogenesis. It directly oxidizes long-chain fatty acids (C7:0–C18:0) and unsaturated fatty acids to methane, integrating β-oxidation with methanogenesis pathways. The archaeon produces 13C-enriched methane, challenging the syntrophic cooperation model and indicating methanogens can independently degrade complex organic substrates in deep subsurface environments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The archaeon oxidizes saturated fatty acids from C7:0 to C18:0 and unsaturated fatty acids like C16:1, C18:1, and C18:2 to produce methane.",
    "Lipotrophic methanogenesis integrates β-oxidation with the Wood-Ljungdahl pathway and methyl-tetrahydromethanopterin:coenzyme M methyltransferase complexes.",
    "Methane from stearate shows moderate 13C-enrichment (δ13C-CH4 = -40.0‰ to -36.3‰), distinct from typical methanogenic pathways."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates methanogens can independently degrade complex organic matter, challenging the classical syntrophic paradigm and refining models of carbon cycling in deep subsurface biospheres."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates electronic bound states in the continuum within a two-dimensional metal using scanning tunneling microscopy. Researchers identified defect-induced localized states in Pd5AlI2, a van der Waals metal, which remain stable within the metallic continuum. The findings suggest electron-hopping interference creates quasi-flat bands, with atomic defects shifting these states into the metallic continuum to form robust, symmetry-protected bound states.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Defect-induced electronic states remain localized within the metallic continuum of Pd5:AlI2",
    "Electron-hopping interference generates quasi-flat bands orthogonal to the dispersive continuum",
    "Atomic defects shift localized states into the metallic continuum, forming symmetry-protected bound states"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates the realization of electronic bound states in the continuum within a two-dimensional metal, providing a pathway to engineer robust quantum states in metallic systems through defect engineering."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates amorphization of organic small molecule 2,3,7,8-tetraamino-5,10-dihydrophenazine-1,4,6,9-tetraone (TDT) to enhance active site exposure in aqueous ammonium-ion batteries. By disrupting π-π stacking, the amorphous TDT achieved a high specific surface area (738 m² g⁻¹), delivered 242.8 mAh g⁻¹ at 0.1 A g⁻¹, and retained 87.1% capacity after 817 cycles. In situ measurements showed NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage. The TDT||CuFe-PBA full cell maintained 100% capacity over 100,000 cycles at 5 A g⁻¹, with an Ah-level pouch cell delivering 1.037 Ah at 1.14 V.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amorphous TDT achieved 738 m² g⁻¹ surface area and 242.8 mAh g⁻¹ capacity at 0.1 A g⁻¹",
    "Amorphous TDT retained 87.1% capacity after 817 cycles and 100% capacity over 100,000 cycles at 5 A g⁻¹",
    "In situ studies revealed NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage mechanisms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "Amorphization of organic small molecules enables high-capacity, durable aqueous ammonium-ion batteries by activating buried redox sites and improving electrolyte accessibility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study analyzed 15 years of Amazonian carbon fluxes using atmospheric CO2 measurements to assess how human activities and droughts impact carbon emissions. It found that deforestation, biomass burning, and climate stressors like El Niño amplify carbon emissions, with forest uptake increasingly failing to offset emissions. The carbon balance shows a net emission of 0.32 ± 0.08 PgC yr-1, driven primarily by fires.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amazon carbon emissions increased to 0.49 ± 0.07 PgC yr-1 during high climate stress years (e.g., El Niño) with significant fire activity",
    "Human-driven deforestation and degradation contributed 0.43 ± 0.13 PgC yr-1 during low climate stress periods",
    "Forest carbon uptake became progressively unable to offset emissions, resulting in a net carbon balance of 0.32 ± 0.08 PgC yr-1"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research demonstrates that human-induced deforestation and climate stressors synergistically amplify Amazon carbon emissions, revealing critical thresholds for forest carbon sink collapse."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the performance of a robotic umpire system designed to call balls and strikes in Major League Baseball. The system's World Series debut highlights its potential for high-stakes applications. The research assesses the robot's precision and reliability in real-world game conditions, though specific metrics are not detailed in the abstract.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The robotic umpire system made its World Series debut",
    "The system requires near-perfect accuracy for high-stakes applications",
    "The study evaluates the robot's precision and reliability in real-game scenarios"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research demonstrates the feasibility of deploying robotic systems for critical sports officiating tasks, advancing the integration of automation in high-precision human activities."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a palladium nanostructure with grain boundaries (PdGB) for humidity-tolerant hydrogen sensing. The researchers developed a sensor operating without external heating that functions across 22°C-80°C and 0%-90% relative humidity. It detects hydrogen at 100 ppm even under high humidity conditions, meeting ISO 2.6142 standards. Mechanistic studies show grain boundaries accelerate palladium hydride formation to weaken water adsorption, enabling reliable operation in humid environments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PdGB sensors operate without external heating across 22°C-80°C and 0%-90% relative humidity",
    "Achieves 100 ppm hydrogen detection limit at 80°C and 90% humidity (261 g m-3 absolute humidity)",
    "Grain boundaries facilitate palladium hydride formation to suppress water interference in hydrogen sensing"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies grain boundaries as a critical design feature for humidity-tolerant catalytic hydrogen sensors, providing a general strategy to overcome water interference in gas sensing applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of fabricating large-scale single-crystal components using additive manufacturing by overcoming thermal constraints through controlled alternating heat inputs. The approach enables metre-tall Ti-6Al-4V single crystals and complex lattice structures, achieving significantly enhanced creep resistance via grain boundary elimination and hierarchical α/β-architecture. The method also extends to refractory metals, broadening the scope of printable single-crystal materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fabrication of metre-tall, centimetre-diameter Ti-6Al-4V single crystals",
    "First single-crystal lattice structures with complex zigzag ligaments",
    "Order-of-magnitude increase in creep resistance over grain-size predictions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable additive manufacturing technique for single-crystal materials, overcoming historical thermal limitations to enable large-scale, complex geometries previously unattainable by conventional methods."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how nanochannel dynamics enhance fast and selective molecular transport under extreme confinement. By leveraging intrinsic mobility like self-rotation, the research demonstrates improved kinetic energy transfer and molecular relays, surpassing current separation benchmarks. The findings emphasize dynamic functionality's role in overcoming frictional and adhesive barriers for efficient mass transport in nanoscale systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nanochannel dynamics enable kinetic energy transfer to improve molecular transport efficiency",
    "Self-rotation of confined functionalities enhances separation performance beyond existing benchmarks",
    "Dynamic functionality overcomes frictional and adhesive barriers in nanoscale confinement"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes nanochannel dynamics as a fundamental mechanism for optimizing mass transport in confined nanoscale systems, advancing understanding of molecular relays and transport selectivity under extreme confinement."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how grain boundary amorphicity influences ionic transport in antiperovskite solid electrolytes using machine learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs). By varying Cl-/Br- ratios and measuring interfacial disorder, the researchers identified a volcano-shaped relationship where intermediate halide compositions optimize ionic conductivity. Cl-enriched boundaries are too ordered, while Br-enriched ones are overly disordered, with optimal performance at moderate amorphicity levels. The findings demonstrate MLIP-enhanced molecular dynamics as a predictive tool for designing low-resistance grain boundaries in solid-state electrolytes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Intermediate Cl-/Br- ratios maximize ionic transport by balancing structural disorder",
    "Cl-enriched grain boundaries exhibit excessive order, limiting ion migration",
    "Br-enriched grain boundaries show excessive disorder, disrupting ionic conduction"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a predictive volcano relationship between grain boundary amorphicity and ionic transport in antiperovskite solid electrolytes, enabling targeted anion engineering for reduced interfacial resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a personal health agent using large language models to integrate multimodal health data from wearable devices and medical records. The agent addresses four user journeys—general health knowledge, data interpretation, wellness advice, and symptom assessment—through three specialized sub-agents: data analysis, health expertise, and coaching. Evaluation across 11 benchmarks with over 7,00:00 annotations demonstrated its capability for personalized health support.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The agent identifies four key user journeys for personalized health interactions",
    "Three specialized sub-agents handle data analysis, health expertise, and coaching",
    "Evaluation across 11 benchmarks with over 7,000 annotations confirmed the system's effectiveness"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive framework for personalized health agents that bridges consumer health data with clinical insights, advancing the field of AI-driven health support systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ultrarapid decision-making in carrion crows using visual motion discrimination tasks. Researchers recorded neural activity in the pallial endbrain to assess decision processes. Crows achieved choices in 235 milliseconds on average, twice as fast as primates without accuracy loss. Direction-selective neurons encoded decisions as early as 70 milliseconds post-stimulus onset, with activity ramping and converging before response.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Carrion c: 235 milliseconds for visual motion discrimination decisions",
    "Direction-selective neurons encode choices 70 milliseconds after stimulus onset",
    "Neural activity ramps with sensory evidence and converges at response onset"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates avian neural circuits can support ultrafast decision-making with high accuracy, revealing evolutionary adaptations for rapid visuomotor responses in birds."
}

{
  "summary": "This review establishes a state-centered framework for organic mixed ionic-electronic conductors (OMIECs), moving beyond scalar descriptors to model electrochemical operation as multidimensional, history-dependent state trajectories. It introduces a minimal sufficient state basis to distinguish essential coordinates, while waveform history and spatial heterogeneity determine when lumped descriptions are valid. The framework enables experimental testing of relationships like congruence and kinetic ordering, and recasts technologies such as electrochromics and electrochemical transistors through a shared electrochemical-state landscape.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A minimal sufficient state basis distinguishes essential from redundant coordinates in OMIECs",
    "Waveform history and spatial heterogeneity define validity of lumped state descriptions",
    "The framework enables experimental testing of congruence, kinetic ordering, and decoupling"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This framework provides a unified approach to model and design electrochemical trajectories in OMIECs, bridging molecular structure, device architecture, and operational protocols for reversible, controllable electrochemical functions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether antiferromagnetic tunnel junctions (AATJs) can exhibit spin-transfer torque effects. Using PtMn3|MgO|PtM. AATJs demonstrated octupole-driven spin-transfer torque (OTT) switching with 363% TMR at room temperature and switching currents near 10 MA cm-2. Theoretical modeling links OTT to spin current imbalances and cluster octupole polarization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AATJs exhibit octupole-driven spin-transfer torque (OTT) switching",
    "363% tunnelling magnetoresistance at room temperature",
    "Switching currents of ~10 MA cm-2"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes antiferromagnetic tunnel junctions as a viable platform for spintronic applications, enabling room-temperature terahertz technologies and deeply scaled magnetic memory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used scanning tunneling microscopy to investigate quantum melting transitions in generalized Wigner crystals (GWCs) and Mott insulators within electron-doped, near-60°-twisted molybdenum diselenide bilayers. The researchers observed electron-hole asymmetry during GWC melting: hole-doped systems formed disordered states driven by interactions, while electron-doped systems transitioned to delocalized liquid-like states. This asymmetry originated from broken particle-hole symmetry in the moiré superlattice, which created distinct electron and hole Fermi pockets with different momentum geometries. The findings provide direct visualization of emergent phases during quantum melting transitions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Electron-hole asymmetry in GWC melting: hole-doped systems exhibit interaction-driven disorder, whereas electron-doped systems form delocalized liquid-like states",
    "Broken particle-hole symmetry in the moiré superlattice generates distinct electron and hole Fermi pockets with different momentum geometries",
    "Mott insulators melt without electron-hole asymmetry, consistent with absent density modulation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study directly visualizes emergent phases during quantum melting transitions in moiré materials, revealing how particle-hole symmetry breaking drives electron-hole asymmetry in correlated systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates thermal radiation engineering by developing a spatial and spectral decoupled meta-window (SSDW) that independently controls broadband thermal radiation's spectral profile and spatial distribution across 8-13 µm. The SSDW achieves visible haze, mid-infrared semitransparency, and suppression of specular reflection while maintaining stable thermal signatures under varying conditions. It enables infrared camouflage and laser-based communication through directional reflection patterns.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SSDW independently controls spectral profile and spatial distribution of broadband thermal radiation (8-13 µm)",
    "Maintains stable thermal signatures despite external-source temperature, incidence angle, and camera viewing angle variations",
    "Encodes 10.6 µm laser incidence direction into spatial reflection patterns for reliable infrared communication"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes spatial and spectral decoupling as a framework for thermal radiation engineering, enabling coordinated control of heat pathways and information transmission beyond traditional spectral manipulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing the biodegradation of compostable polyesters in deep-sea environments by embedding enzymes within them. The researchers thermally integrated enzymes into four types of polyesters (PBS, PBSA, PCL, PBAT) and tested their degradation in coastal and deep-sea settings up to 5,503 meters. Results showed near-complete degradation at 757 meters within five months, with significant biodegradation observed at extreme depths. The approach maintains mechanical properties while enabling rapid marine breakdown.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Enzyme-embedded polyesters achieved near-complete degradation at 757 m deep-sea depth within 5 months",
    "Moderate biodegradation occurred at extreme depths of 5,503 m despite harsh conditions",
    "The embedded enzymes enabled rapid degradation in coastal seawater with minimal enzyme concentration (0.1 wt%)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy provides a scalable method for accelerating marine biodegradation of compostable plastics, addressing a critical gap in deep-sea plastic pollution mitigation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the long-term ecological impact of the 2010 Deepwater Horizon oil spill on Gulf of Mexico marine ecosystems. Using a 13-year longitudinal analysis, researchers assessed ecosystem recovery status. Findings indicate persistent ecological disruption, with no significant recovery observed in the studied areas despite 13 years post-spill.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No significant recovery of Gulf of Mexico marine ecosystems 13 years after the Deepwater Horizon oil spill",
    "Persistent ecological disruption in the study areas",
    "Long-term ecological impact of the oil spill continues to affect marine environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research provides critical evidence that deep-sea ecosystems remain ecologically perturbed decades after major oil spills, highlighting the long-term consequences of such environmental disasters."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates engineering the Sn4+/Sn2+ redox reaction in aqueous zinc-ion batteries using cesium tin iodide perovskites. The approach involves in situ growth of single and double perovskite layers on the cathode, enabling the first demonstration of the Sn4+/Sn2+ redox couple. Results show increased potential to 0.39 V vs. SHE, dual discharge plateaus, high areal capacity, and exceptional cycling stability in full batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "First demonstration of Sn4+/Sn2+ redox reaction in aqueous zinc-ion batteries",
    "Increased redox potential to 0.39 V vs. SHE via enhanced tin-halide coordination",
    "High areal capacity (0.80 mAh cm-2) and long cycling stability (7000 cycles at 16 mA cm-2)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work enables high-potential redox reactions in aqueous zinc-ion batteries through perovskite interlayers, advancing energy storage technology with enhanced capacity and stability."
}
